<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<component type="desktop-application">
  <id>io.github.mehmetnuri.Ferry</id>
  <metadata_license>CC0-1.0</metadata_license>
  <project_license>GPL-3.0-or-later</project_license>
  <name>Ferry</name>
  <summary>Move files to and from servers and cloud storage</summary>
  <developer id="io.github.mehmetnuri">
    <name>Mehmet Nuri Öztürk</name>
  </developer>
  <description>
    <p>
      Ferry moves files between your computer and file servers or cloud storage: SFTP,
      FTP, WebDAV and Nextcloud, Google Drive, Azure Blob Storage, Amazon S3, Cloudflare R2, MinIO, Supabase
      Storage and other S3-compatible services.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>Browse buckets and file servers in a list or a grid with thumbnails; folders open instantly from a cache</li>
      <li>SFTP also through a jump host, with the SSH agent and checked server keys; FTP over TLS; WebDAV and Nextcloud</li>
      <li>Cryptomator vaults, unlocked right in the window on any bucket or server</li>
      <li>Quick preview of images, videos, audio and text with the space key</li>
      <li>A transfer queue with priorities, pausing each transfer, speed limit and retries; interrupted uploads and downloads continue where they stopped</li>
      <li>Recent objects of every connection, sorting, and downloading folders as one ZIP file</li>
      <li>Opens s3:// links from anywhere in the desktop; previews highlighted code, CSV tables and ZIP contents</li>
      <li>Copy in Ferry and paste in GNOME Files; mounted buckets appear among the bookmarks</li>
      <li>Copy, cut and paste, moving by drag and drop with undo, batch rename</li>
      <li>Upload by drag and drop or by pasting files copied in GNOME Files, with conflict handling</li>
      <li>Share links with QR codes, and upload links for people without an account</li>
      <li>Find objects from the GNOME Shell overview</li>
      <li>Object versions, permissions, Object Lock, bucket policy, CORS, lifecycle and CloudFront</li>
      <li>Folder sync, scheduled backup jobs and mounting a bucket as a folder</li>
      <li>Storage analyzer and a compatibility test for any S3-compatible provider</li>
      <li>Credentials kept in the system keyring; AWS CLI profiles with single sign-on, assumed roles with MFA codes</li>
      <li>Connection backups protected with a password, age or SSH keys, a YubiKey or a GnuPG key</li>
      <li>Servers with self-signed certificates or a private certificate authority, after checking the fingerprint</li>
      <li>Pauses while offline and keeps the computer awake during transfers</li>
    </ul>
  </description>
